<h2 id="why-use-them">Why use them <a class="heading-anchor" href="#why-use-them" aria-label="Permalink to Why use them">#</a></h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>They sound like themselves.</strong> Voice rules, address terms and guardrails are part of the repository, not a one-line prompt.</li>
  <li><strong>They share your archive.</strong> The Grimoire gives them the same books, lines and items you can look up.</li>
  <li><strong>They can check a quote.</strong> The archive's <code>verify</code> command is part of the workflow.</li>
  <li><strong>They can use MCP.</strong> Connect the MCP server and the persona can search the archive as a tool.</li>
  <li><strong>They can ask each other.</strong> A read-only consult copy lets one character ask another a question without sharing private notes.</li>
</ul>

